Customers log in with a single-use link by email through django-sesame, in `<package>/magic_link.py`.
The team creates their accounts in the admin, with an unusable password.
Staff, superusers and accounts with a password receive no link: a mailbox alone must not open them.
A link works once, within 15 minutes (`SESAME_MAX_AGE`), and keeps a local `next`.
It opens a page whose button logs in: mail scanners such as Outlook's Safe Links fetch links first.
An account receives one link per minute, and the page answers the same for unknown addresses.
