{% raw %}## Tests

Tests use Django's test framework with django-test-plus and model-bakery.
The test runner in `<package>/test_runner.py` adds rich output.
It also swaps the manifest static storage for a plain one, so tests need no `collectstatic`.
It sets the default task backend to `ImmediateBackend`, so enqueued tasks run inside the test.
Write a failing test before a fix or a feature.

## Production

The Docker image runs `manage.py serve`, granian over ASGI on port 8000, and migrates on start.
Before that it runs `check --deploy`, which stops the start on errors but not on warnings.
Deployments run behind Caddy, which terminates TLS and compresses responses.
Outside `DEBUG`, granian serves `STATIC_ROOT` itself with a one-year cache.
`collectstatic` keeps only files with a content hash in their name, plus the manifest.
The storage is `<package>/storage.py`.
Reference static files only through `{% static %}`; a hard-coded `/static/...` path gets a 404.
In `DEBUG`, Django serves static files from the app directories without `collectstatic`.
`GRANIAN_*` environment variables configure granian, such as `GRANIAN_WORKERS`.
granian waits for open responses when it stops, and a server-sent event stream stays open.
`manage.py serve` therefore kills a worker that has not stopped after 5 seconds, or 1 with `--reload`.
`GRANIAN_WORKERS_KILL_TIMEOUT` overrides that.
Every open stream is one request, and granian handles `GRANIAN_BACKPRESSURE` requests per worker at once.
granian's default is its backlog of 1024 divided by the workers.
`manage.py serve` sets 8192 per worker instead; `GRANIAN_BACKPRESSURE` overrides it.
{% endraw %}{% if background_tasks %}{% raw %}The arguments `worker` and `scheduler` start the task worker and the scheduler from the same image.
Only the web process migrates, so start the others after it.
On the first SIGTERM the worker finishes its current task, then exits.
Docker sends SIGKILL after 10 seconds, which leaves a longer task `RUNNING`.
Set the worker's `stop_grace_period` in Compose above the runtime of the longest task.
{% endraw %}{% endif %}{% raw %}`SECRET_KEY` and `ALLOWED_HOSTS` must be set outside `DEBUG`.

`GET /health` answers `{"status": "ok"}` without touching the database.
`GET /health/ready` also checks the database and the cache, and answers 503 when one fails.
`<package>/health.py` answers both before host validation, the HTTPS redirect, sessions and CSRF.
A health check on the loopback therefore passes without an entry in `ALLOWED_HOSTS`.
